2018-03-22 [high] LagrangianBlock, LagrangianFunction

	SMS++ is motivated by decomposition: we should verify that it
	is indeed possible to simplify the development of decomposition
	algorithms, starting from Lagrangian ones. The best would be to
	have a C05Function::LagrangianFunction that has a Block with a
	Solver attached and a bunch of free-floating functions (cf.
	Observers) and implements the C05Function with all its methods and
	modifications.

	Then, it seems it would make sense to have LagrangianBlock
	defining the Lagrangian multipliers (with the corresponding
	constraints, e.g. non-negativity, if needed) and having a bunch
	of LagrangianFunctions to represent the Lagrangian Dual of
	something, although I'm not 100% sure it is really needed.
	One good reason for doing this is, if possible, to implement once
	and for all at least some of the methods for passing information
	back and forth between the original Block and its Lagrangian
	Function/Dual.


2018-03-22 [medium, pre-requisite LagrangianBlock] LagrangianUCBlock

	Simply, the concrete implementation of get_r3_Block() in
	UCBlock that produces the Lagrangian dual w.r.t. the energy
	constraints, with all the methods to pass information back and
	forth between this and the original one.


